    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4786" root="ثنى" body-key="v">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُثَنًّى</span></b>  [pass. part. n. of 2. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>Dualized:</i> a <i>dual.</i>
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُثَنَّاةٌ فَوْقِيَّةٌ</span> <i>Marked with two points above:</i>
an epithet added to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تآء</span> to prevent its being mistaken for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بآء</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثآء</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يآء</span>. And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُثَنَّاةٌ تَحْتِيَّةٌ</span> <i>Marked
with two points below:</i> an epithet added to <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">يآء</span> to
prevent its being mistaken for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بآء</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تآء</span> or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثآء</span>.]
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الطَّويلُ المُثَنَّى</span> (assumed tropical:)  <i>That which passes away</i> [<i>out
of sight,</i> or <i>disappears,</i>] <i>by length;</i> mostly used
of a thing that is long without breadth. (TA.)

